    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0820" n="798" xml:id="pg798"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/3–550: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Legation in Jordan </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-03-09T19:00:00-05:00">March 9, 1950—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Ur 38 Mar 5 and previous. Dept disappointed by recent developments
                    culminating in setback for King in his efforts bring conversations with Israel
                    to concrete conclusion. If you believe such action wld be helpful, you are
                    authorized convey to King an expression of Dept’s appreciation for efforts he
                    has so far made on behalf peace and stability in Palestine, and of Dept’s hope
                    that King will continue seek agreement. You might refer to President’s msg of
                    encouragement to King sent Deptel 216 Dec 30, 1949.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d400-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>In your discretion you are also authorized discreetly to encourage members of
                    Jordan Govt re desirability of continuing conversations with Israelis in effort
                    arrive at satisfactory formula for agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d400-f1" n="1" xml:id="d400-f1-content">
                <p>This message gave the text of President Truman’s message to King Abdullah; see
                        <ref target="frus1949v06#pg_1564">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1949, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, p. 1564</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
